<% content_for :title, "Printable daily routine sheet for an elderly parent" %>
<% content_for :description, "A free one-page daily routine sheet to print and put on the fridge: medication times, meals, and the phone numbers worth having to hand. No signup needed." %>

<div class="no-print">
  <h1>A daily routine sheet you can print</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    One page for the fridge door. Fill it in by hand, print a fresh one when the
    routine changes, and leave it somewhere it will actually be seen. Useful on
    its own — there is nothing to sign up for.
  </p>

  <p>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" onclick="window.print()">Print this sheet</button>
    <span class="print-hint">or press Ctrl+P — ⌘P on a Mac.</span>
  </p>

  <hr class="rule">
</div>

<%#
  Everything below is what actually prints: large type, generous rules to write
  on, and no navigation. The print stylesheet in the marketing layout hides the
  site header, footer and .no-print blocks.
%>
<section class="sheet">
  <h2 class="sheet-title">Daily routine for <span class="fill fill-name"></span></h2>

  <table class="sheet-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Time</th><th>What happens</th><th>Done</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% 8.times do %>
        <tr><td class="fill"></td><td class="fill"></td><td class="tick"></td></tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3 class="sheet-heading">Medication</h3>
  <table class="sheet-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Medicine</th><th>Dose</th><th>When</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% 6.times do %>
        <tr><td class="fill"></td><td class="fill"></td><td class="fill"></td></tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3 class="sheet-heading">If something is wrong, ring</h3>
  <table class="sheet-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Who</th><th>Number</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% 4.times do %>
        <tr><td class="fill"></td><td class="fill"></td></tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>

<div class="no-print">
  <hr class="rule">

  <p>
    If keeping the sheet up to date turns into its own chore,
    <a href="<%= login_path %>">Remindly</a> does the same job out loud: you set
    the times from your own phone, it speaks each one at their end, and it emails
    you when a dose is taken or missed. It is free.
    <a href="<%= faq_path %>">The questions page</a> covers what it does and does
    not do.
  </p>

  <%= render "shared/subscribe_form", source: "routine_sheet" %>
</div>
